Upgrade procedure for bmake

Source: https://ftp.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/misc/sjg/bmake-VERSION.tar.gz
        (also http://www.crufty.net/ftp/pub/sjg/bmake-VERSION.tar.gz)

The vendor branch vendor/NetBSD/bmake holds the unpacked upstream tarball at
the repository root; the in-tree copy lives at contrib/bmake.

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download and extract bmake-VERSION.tar.gz (it unpacks into bmake/).
2. Use the vendor-update skill: rsync the tree into a worktree on
   vendor/NetBSD/bmake, commit "Vendor import of bmake VERSION", tag
   vendor/NetBSD/bmake/VERSION.
3. Merge into master with

       git subtree merge -P contrib/bmake vendor/NetBSD/bmake

4. Re-apply the local patches listed below (FreeBSD's contrib/bmake carries
   the same job.c/make.1/meta2deps.sh patches, so its copies can be used
   directly when FreeBSD is on the same bmake version).
5. Refresh usr.bin/bmake from FreeBSD's usr.bin/bmake (Makefile,
   Makefile.config, Makefile.inc, config.h, unit-tests/Makefile,
   unit-tests/Makefile.config), keeping the MidnightBSD differences noted
   below.  config.h is the output of configure on FreeBSD and is valid for
   MidnightBSD as well.
6. Build usr.bin/bmake, run "make test" there with the new binary, build a
   few programs and libraries with it, and finally do a buildworld since
   make is the bootstrap tool.

Local patches applied on top of upstream:

  - job.c (FreeBSD): .MAKE.ALWAYS_PASS_JOB_QUEUE (pass the job token pipe
    to all children, not only .MAKE targets; default yes) and
    MAKE_JOB_ERROR_TOKEN (do not deposit an error token when set to no, so
    one failing architecture does not abort a tinderbox).  Hunks in
    JobExec(), Job_Init() and JobTokenAdd().
  - make.1 (FreeBSD): document .MAKE.ALWAYS_PASS_JOB_QUEUE and cross
    reference style.Makefile(5).
  - mk/meta2deps.sh (FreeBSD): example path comments updated.
  - mk/lib.mk, mk/prog.mk, mk/own.mk: treat TARGET_OSNAME/_HOST_OSNAME
    "MidnightBSD" like "FreeBSD" (ELF shared library rules, dynamic linker
    options, CPPFLAGS handling, :NFreeBSD:NNetBSD filters).
  - unit-tests/export.mk: FILTER_CMD also drops CODEQL_*, LD_PRELOAD and
    SEMMLE_* so the export test passes under CodeQL tracing.
  - bmake.cat1: regenerated with
        mandoc -Tascii -Ios="MidnightBSD X.Y" bmake.1 > bmake.cat1
    so the header and footer say MidnightBSD.

usr.bin/bmake differences from FreeBSD:

  - Makefile: CLEANDIRS+= FreeBSD MidnightBSD
  - Makefile.inc: no "MK_host_egacy= no" (MidnightBSD has no host_egacy
    knob); keeps the MK_SHARED_TOOLCHAIN / NO_SHARED block.

Notes:

  - Upstream removed lst.lib/, nonints.h, sprite.h and strlist.[ch] long
    ago; they must not be resurrected by a merge.
  - The in-tree manual page is generated from contrib/bmake/make.1 (see
    usr.bin/bmake/Makefile, MK_GEN_MAN).
